.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt RENICE 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm renice
.Nd alter the nice value of a process, process group or user
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n
.Ar priority
.Op Fl p | Fl g | Fl u
.Ar id ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
sets the absolute nice value
.Ar priority
for each target and prints the resulting value as
.Dq Li id: value .
The kernel enforces the same permission rules as
.Xr setpriority 2 :
an unprivileged caller may only lower its own niceness.
.Pp
The default selector is a process id.
.Fl g
selects a process group and
.Fl u
a user id.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl n
Take the priority from the following argument.
.It Fl p
Select process ids.
.It Fl g
Select process-group ids.
.It Fl u
Select user ids.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A target failure exits 1; a usage error exits 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nice 1 ,
.Xr getpriority 2
.Sh STANDARDS
IEEE Std 1003.1-2024
.Pq POSIX.1-2024 .
